`createCompressionGroup` now filters `queryByIds` results by the incoming `topicId` before anything else:

```ts
const rawMessages = await this.messageModel.queryByIds(messageIds, { postProcessUrl });
const messagesToSummarize = rawMessages.filter((msg) => msg.topicId === topicId);
const scopedMessageIds = messagesToSummarize.map((msg) => msg.id);
```

The filtered `scopedMessageIds` list is then used for **both** the summarization payload and `compressionRepository.createCompressionGroup({ messageIds })`, so `markMessagesAsCompressed` can only touch messages that belong to the active topic. A request that tries to mix in IDs from another topic (crafted or malformed) will have those IDs silently dropped; if nothing remains after filtering, we throw instead of creating an empty group.

`queryByIds` itself still scopes by `userId`, so cross-user contamination was already impossible — this change closes the remaining cross-topic / same-user gap.
